{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:e02c2bf6b108e72fe2a7b64d87224e40a243db1b","text":"Withdrawn rather than left for Hugh to ratify, because ratifying it now would create a charter the connector refuses.\n\nTwo things changed under it since it was proposed. It carries an empty body, and the connector now requires a charter to name the connector, owner, repository and actor, refusing one that names none of them — so this would be admitted by the fold and then rejected at the doorstep, which is the worst of both. And it is premised on the inbound charter f696c18a, which Hugh has since retired and replaced with the scoped b86860f2, so its stated scope refers to something no longer live.\n\nThe outbound half is not blocked by this withdrawal. It is blocked on the inbound half reaching main, and the charter for it should be stated once that work has settled what it actually needs to authorize — which is the order I argued for in the promise at b0fdeacd: build the half, let its shape decide the charter, then have an operator state and ratify a scoped one."}